#!/bin/bash
# ending plates that avoid showing the child's body (the video models' safety filter refused it in round 1)
cd /hutian/repo
S="soft gouache and watercolour storybook illustration, 19th-century Danish fairy-tale picture book, visible paper grain and dry-brush texture, painterly, not photoreal, not 3D, not anime, no text, no lettering, no watermark."
COR="the same snowy corner nook as the reference: the LEFT ochre-stucco house stands further out with a closed shuttered door, the RIGHT rust-grey stucco house is set back, the back wall rough cracked wet-stone grey plaster with scrape marks, worn stone step, deep snow drifted in the angle"
g(){ python3 tools/gen.py "$@" || python3 tools/gen.py "$@"; }
g refs/ending/end_remains.png "$COR, at DAWN in pale grey-blue and faint rose light, gentle snowfall, NO people at all. On the stone step lies a thin dark-grey shawl folded and dusted with snow, beside it a small bundle of burnt black matches tied with twine and a few spent matches in the snow. A very faint warm golden glow rests on the cracked wall where she had struck her matches, as if light lingers. Tender, quiet, still. $S" refs/corner_dawn.png &
g refs/ending/end_townspeople_backs.png "Seen from behind in pale dawn light: three or four 1840s Danish townspeople in long dark wool coats, a top hat, bonnets and a woman in a dove-grey bonnet and dark-green coat, standing together at the open end of the snowy corner nook, looking down toward the foot of the cracked stone wall; the thing they look at is hidden behind their coats and is not shown. Snow falling gently, pale grey-blue and faint rose. Muted solemn mood, no faces visible. ${COR}. $S" refs/corner_dawn.png refs/cast_boy_passers.png &
g refs/ending/end_boots_shadows.png "Low camera near the snow, pale dawn light: the boots, shoe buckles and long coat hems of several townspeople walking slowly across deep snow toward a cobbled corner nook between two stucco houses, their long soft blue shadows stretching ahead of them onto the cracked stone wall; a few burnt matches lie in the snow in the foreground. No faces, no bodies above the knees. Pale grey-blue and faint rose. $S" refs/corner_dawn.png &
g refs/ending/end_woman_hand.png "Close-up in pale dawn light: the gloved hand of a woman in a dove-grey bonnet and dark-green coat, in profile, her other hand pressed gently to her chest, eyes lowered and sorrowful but kind, looking down out of frame; she holds a small bundle of burnt black matches she has picked up from the snow. Softly falling snow, pale grey-blue and faint rose, shallow depth, painted. $S" refs/cast_boy_passers.png refs/corner_dawn.png &
g refs/ending/end_sky_dawn.png "Rising view above the snow-covered gabled rooftops and chimneys of a small 1840s Danish town at sunrise: chimney smoke rising straight, the sky pale grey-rose at the bottom turning to faint gold at the top, a few last stars fading, and high in the glowing sky two tiny soft white-gold points of light close together drifting upward and dissolving. No people. Hopeful, serene, quiet. $S" refs/street_dusk.png refs/ascent.png &
g refs/ending/end_girl_far.png "Very wide, distant view at dawn: the snowy corner nook between two stucco houses seen from far down the street, in pale grey-blue and faint rose light; a small group of townspeople in dark coats stands at its mouth, and just beyond them a tiny, peaceful, snow-dusted figure of the girl (fair curls, blue checked apron, dark shawl) wrapped in snow at the foot of the wall like a sleeping child, only a few brush strokes of detail, no face visible, not graphic. $S" refs/corner_dawn.png refs/dawn_girl.png &
wait
